      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem better than the previous version to me.  It\u0027s even longer, and with the added complexity of trying to figure out how `binary.Write` will handle the assorted types in `data`.  I\u0027d suggest either 4 calls to `binary.Write`, or skip the `bytes.Buffer` and use the equivalent byte slice directly\n\n```\nvar buf []byte\nbuf \u003d binary.LittleEndian.AppendUint16(buf, Sha256HeaderID)\nbuf \u003d binary.LittleEndian.AppendUint16(buf, uint16(dataSize))\nbuf \u003d binary.LittleEndian.AppendUint16(buf, Sha256HeaderSignature)\nbuf \u003d append(buf, checksum...)\n```",
